Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 12 28 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma with extensive extracellular mucin and DCIS on right side  Right breast cancer  long stitch equals lateral  short stitch equals deep                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 1  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR INFERIOR INTERFACE MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 17 38                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm yellow and tan soft tissue fragment  The entire specimen is frozen as FX 1  now submitted in cassette A  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a short black stitch designating the deep  and a long black stitch designating the lateral margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm unremarkable gray tan skin ellipse at the superficial aspect superiorly  The deep margin is inked black  the superficial blue  the superior green  and the inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm hemorrhagic cavity with surrounding chalky tan yellow areas consistent with fat necrosis  The cavity comes to 0 1cm of the superior  0 2cm of the superficial  anterior end   0 3cm of the deep  posterior   0 3cm of the inferior  1 8cm of the lateral  and 1 2cm of the medial margins  The remaining cut surface shows dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted from lateral to medial as B H  with the lateral margin radially sectioned as B  the medial margin as H  and the entire cavity as C G  Resident  TRACY L  DAVIS  MD   Ph D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  DAVID COON  PhD  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINAL   EXCISION PART B  BREAST RIGHT  RE EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 MAY 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 MAY 95 at 16 05 CLINICAL DATA  46 year old female with right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  1 7 CM   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  PRESENT A FRACTION OF A MM FROM AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH FIBROSIS  MICROCYSTS  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  No ductal carcinoma in situ is identified  AXILLA  RIGHT   RESECTION  CARCINOMA METASTATIC TO 3 OF 16 LYMPH NODES  3 16   Diagnosis by  Jeoffry Brennick  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 47 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS  BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two separate specimens   Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm unoriented breast excision specimen  inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan  firm  somewhat well defined mass  extending to less than 1mm from an inked resection margin  Representative sections in A D  Next to the periphery of the lesion is a tan  soft  ill defined area which extends to the inked margin  representative section in E   Right axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary lymph node dissection containing multiple nodules  REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm in greatest diameter  representative sections in F J  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART A  BREAST MASS  RIGHT  PART B  AXILLA  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
