Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 92 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 17 30 CLINICAL DATA  82 year old woman with right arm swelling and a breast mass  had a biopsy in REMOVED_MONTH of  REMOVED_CASE_ID  which revealed infiltrating ductal carcinoma   grade REMOVED_DATE The patient has been on chemotherapy for six months                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  1  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  10   AND INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  2 FOCI  MICROSCOPIC AND REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The 2 foci of infiltrating carcinoma and multiple foci of intraductal carcinoma are located away from the biopsy cavity  Carcinoma is not present within the biopsy cavity  Lymphatic invasion is present  The inked resection margins are free of carcinoma  2  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 3 OF 3 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  EACH WITH EXTENSION THROUGH THE CAPSULE INTO AXILLARY ADIPOSE TISSUE  AN ADDITIONAL 8 TUMOR NODULES DEVOID OF LYMPHOID TISSUE ARE PRESENT WITHIN THE AXILLARY TISSUE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor nodules may represent lymph nodes completely replaced by tumor  3  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  4  FOREIGN BODY GIANT REACTION  FIBROSIS AND FAT NECROSIS CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY SITE  SKIN WITH SCAR AND SKIN TAG  Diagnosis by  Deborah S  Fleischhacker  MD ScD Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 12 23                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a 30 x 15 x 6cm right modified radical mastectomy with a 22 x 7 x 2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue at one end  A 30 x 7cm skin ellipse overlying the breast tissue contains a 6 0cm long well healed scar at one end of the skin ellipse and a 4 5cm in diameter areola at the opposite end of the skin ellipse  In the center of the areola with a 1 0cm in diameter unremarkable nipple 0 5cm inferior to the nipple is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm apparent acrochordon on the areola  1 7cm from the areolar margin  Also received in the same container is a separate 15 x 4 5cm skin ellipse  with 2cm of underlying adipose tissue  Both the skin and the adipose tissue are unremarkable  The mastectomy specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm area of fibrous tissue beneath the scar  The fibrous tissue beneath the scar extends to 3 5cm from the deep resection margin and 3 0cm from the closest lateral resection margin  Within the remainder of the breast parenchyma are focal areas of rubbery tan breast parechyma  No firm  stellate  or gritty area are identified  SECTION CODE  A  skin with scar B  nipple C  acrochordon on areola D G  sections of biopsy site with inked margins H M  additional sections of breast parenchyma distant from biopsy site N U  lymph nodes from axillary tale V  representative section of separate skin ellipse  Resident  Jeoffry Brennick  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  David Bent Smith  M D  James M Fitzgerald  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST AND AXILLA   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 33 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  PLEOMORPHIC   REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN AND INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not identified  The tumor does not invade skeletal muscle  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 38                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a previously opened REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of breast containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fairly well circumscribed  hard  tan white nodule  less than 0 1cm from the inked surface  Representative frozen is as frozen section  1  and resubmitted in cassette H  The remainder is submitted in A through G  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
