xty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 47 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm breast tissue fragment with a wire in place with accompanied x ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal a fibrofatty cut surface with many small firm nodules scattered throughout  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm  tan yellow stellate mass is identified  0 5cm from the inked resection margin  A representative section of the tumor is frozen as frozen section  1 save frozen  The mass is entirely in A through E  representative section of the remainder in F through J  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DCIS  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST  BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
