Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Resident  Russell Ryan  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 40 year old woman with a history of left breast cancer  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MULTIPLE MICROSCOPIC FOCI RANGING FROM SINGLE CELLS TO REMOVED_DATE CM  IN TOTAL AGGREGATING TO APPROXIMATELY REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE INKED MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT   SEE NOTE   2  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  EXTENSIVE  PRESENT IN 11 OF 13 TISSUE BLOCKS AND PRESENT AT THE INKED MARGIN OF RESECTION IN SEVERAL FOCI AND PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT IN MULTIPLE FOCI  NOTE  The invasive and in situ carcinoma is present in the main  largest  specimen as well as in the smaller tissue fragments submitted in the same container  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm breast excisional biopsy specimen with a needle localization wire passing into one aspect and along the long axis of the specimen  The specimen is unoriented  It is correlated with the specimen radiograph which shows a cylindrical  radiopaque object in the vicinity of the needle localization wire  Also received in the same container are two separate portions of fibrofatty breast tissue  the larger measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm and the other  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the long axis into 10 sections numbered REMOVED_DATE with  1 containing the aspect through which the needle localization wire passed  On cut section  the specimen is primarily fibrous with a 0 5cm diameter  hemorrhagic cavity consistent with biopsy cavity present at one edge margin  sections 3 6   A 0 2cm metal cylinder is found within this cavity in section  6  Two additional fragments of breast tissue are inked blue externally  serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section  1  radial to end margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections  2 9  entire specimen  one per cassette   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section  10  radially to end margin  specimen entirely submitted    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Larger separate fragment  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Smaller separate fragment  entirely submitted  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1  Immunohistochemical stains for keratin  p63  calponin and myosin were performed on a representative section of the tumor and confirm the presence of in situ and invasive ductal carcinoma  Addendum  1 by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 09 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO INKED MARGIN  NOTE  Tumor extensively involves most of the tissue submitted  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 47                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT  BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   3   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 56     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm mass of fibroadipose tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a homogeneous tan  finely granular surface  Representative sections frozen as frozen section  1  The frozen block is sent to Cox 5 for estrogen and progesterone receptor analysis  Sections sent for BRDU  Remainder is submitted in cassettes A and B  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
