Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 33 CLINICAL DATA  29 year old female with right breast carcinoma  grade III  and left breast ductal carcinoma in situ  Status post left lumpectomy with positive margins                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  COMEDO TYPE  EXTENSIVELY PRESENT ON 7 OF 8 SECTIONS  WITH A MAXIMUM MEASURED SPAN OF REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE TO MULTIPLE MARGINS  Note  No stromal  lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL LATERAL    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  EXTENSIVELY PRESENT ON 4 OF 5 SECTIONS  WITH A MAXIMUM MEASURED SPAN OF REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE NEW  TRUE  MARGINS  Note  No stromal  lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 25                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Two specimens are received fresh  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Designated  left breast tumor  long stitch lateral  is an oriented 6 x 4 x 2 5cm breast tissue with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm skin ellipse  with a short and long stitch  There is a 1 6cm well healed scar in the skin ellipse  The entire excised surface is inked black  and over inked according to the following  superior  blue  lateral  red  medial  yellow  and inferior  green  Cross sectioning reveals a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm biopsy cavity filled with red brown  gelatinous material  The tissue on one side of the biopsy cavity is firm and fibrous  diffusely extending into the surrounding breast parenchyma  The other side has yellow white  opaque discoloration  forming a 1cm rim along the biopsy cavity  The biopsy appears to extend to the inferior excised margin  This margin is in A  Sections from the biopsy cavity are in B through G  Parenchyma away from biopsy cavity is in H  Designated  additional lateral tissue  long equals new lateral margin  short equals superior  is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm fragment of breast tissue with a long and short stitch  The new lateral excised surface is inked black  and the medial inked red  Cross sectioning reveals firm  white tissue with cystic changes admixed with adipose tissue  Fully submitted in I through M  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael V Seiden  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL LATERAL    EXCISIONAL BIO PART B  BREAST  LEFT TUMOR   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
