settes P Y  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margins  medial  right breast  is a fibroadipose specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The unoriented specimen is unoriented  serially sectioned and submitted in cassettes Z GG  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margins  lateral  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x up to 1 5cm fibroadipose tissue specimen which is unoriented  The specimen is inked black  serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes HH NN  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shave margins  superior  right breast  are 3 fibroadipose tissue fragments measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes OO RR  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary lymph node  right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm adipose tissue mass containing 5 lymph nodes submitted as follows  SS  1 lymph node bivalved  TT  2 lymph nodes bivalved  UU  Adiposee tissue  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional right axillary lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm lymph node with minor amount of additional adipose tissue  The lymph node is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes VV WW  Resident  MASSIMO D APUZZO  MD PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 2  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWO NODES  O R  Resident  NICOLE ANN BELSLEY  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  RE