in faintly for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 16 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node right hot and blue  REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan red lymph node that is trisected and entirely frozen as FX  1 now resubmitted into cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is an oriented right simple mastectomy specimen with a short stitch denoting the superior margin and a long stitch denoting the lateral margin  The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm and has a REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm elliptical portion of skin with a 4 0cm diameter unremarkable nipple areola complex  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm region of blue green discoloration in the center of the skin ellipse  No scars are noted  The posterior margin is inked black and the anterior margin is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm fibrous area in the 10 o clock region of the breast which is tan red  granular and  slightly nodular  It is 2 9cm from the posterior margin and approximately 1 5cm from the anterior margin  Adjacent to this area is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan white  hard stellate nodule which is 0 9cm from the closest  anterior  margin  Inferior is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm hard nodule which is 4 5cm from the posterior resection margin  Also noted in the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm tan red  granular  and firm area in the 1 o clock portion of the breast  This area is 3 5cm from the posterior margin and 3 1cm from the anterior skin  The surrounding uninvolved breast parenchyma is predominantly yellow  lobulated  and fatty with focal areas of more tan white and firm fibrous tissue  The lateral portion of the specimen is explored and no lymph nodes are present  Representative sections are submitted as per section code  Section Code  B E U Y  Representative sections of 10 o clock area  F  Closest posterior margin to 10 o clock area  G  10 o clock area to nearest anterior margin  H K  Z DD  Firm 1 o clock area  L  Closest posterior margin to 1 o clock area  M P  Medial breast  Q  Hard 0 5cm nodule inferior to the 10 o clock area  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional right axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fragment of yellow fibrofatty tissue containing scattered small lymph nodes  All individual lymph nodes present in the specimen are submitted into cassette R  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  axillary skin tag  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm polypoid fragment of tan and wrinkled skin which is bisected and entirely submitted into cassette S  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  inframammary skin tag  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of tan and wrinkled polypoid skin which is bisected and entirely submitted into cassette T  Resident  PAUL MICHAELS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  STEWART M  KNOEPP  MD   Ph D  O R  Diagnosis by  William C  Faquin MD PhD                          