rounding the cavity is firm  light yellow tissue that is surrounded by soft yellow lobulated tissue  The cavity comes to within 0 5cm of the deepest posterior inked margin  The cavity begins 1cm unbeneath the skin scar  The breast parenchyma posterior and medial to the nipple and medial is firm and gray and focally hemorrhagic  The skin and nipple are unremarkable  Six lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary fat pad  The largest is 3 x 1 x 1cm and contains focal green yellow soft tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Two representative sections of the largest lymph nodes are submitted  The five smaller nodes are submitted in toto  one per cassette  Section Code A F   representative breast parenchyma surrounding cavity G H   representative parenchyma posterior and medial to nipple I   deepest resection margin J   nipple K   largest lymph node L P   smaller lymph nodes in toto  one per cassette  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  John Daniel Puskas  M D  James M Fitzgerald  M D  Rex Neal Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST AND AXILLARY NODES   report_end  , Unchecked.
