ISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 15 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm left mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm irregular portion of tan skin with an eccentric unremarkable nipple and a 5 0cm well healed  linear scar running from superior to inferior  Connected to this ellipse of skin is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm strip of tan skin along the inferior aspect that contains a 13 5cm linear  well healed scar  There is a short stitch on the superior aspect and a long stitch on the lateral aspect  Within the parenchyma there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm poorly circumscribed white firm mass with an irregular REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm extension  The mass is less than 0 1cm from the deep margin  and 0 8cm from the anterior superior margin  1 5cm medial to this mass  there is a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm hard firm white mass that is 1 0cm from the deep margin and 2 0cm from the closest anterior superior margin  The remainder of the parenchyma is notable for several small  discrete firm white nodules ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 9cm  these are scattered throughout the parenchyma and focally come to 0 1cm from the deep margin and 0 4cm from the anterior margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE  A  Main mass to anterior margin  B  Main mass to posterior margin  C  Irregular extension of main mass to posterior margin  D  Representative sections of main mass  E  Representative sections of second nodule  F  Closest posterior margin to second nodule  G  Discrete small nodule to posterior margin  H  Discrete small nodule to anterior inferior margin  I J  Representative sections of fibrous parenchyma away from masses  with ink representing posterior  Within the axillary fat multiple tan lymph nodes are identified  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in greatest dimension  Whole nodes are submitted in K N  and representative sections of nodes are submitted in O Q  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional nodal tissue   are 3 tan nodules  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The larger nodule is bisected and submitted entirely in R  and the smaller nodules are submitted entirely in S  Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES   ADDITIONAL     report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 52 CLINICAL DATA  None given                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90   WELL TO MODERATE DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO INKED MARGINS    INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  10    MIXED CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID SUBTYPES     ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 8cm in greatest diameter  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Dr Koerner has reviewed this case and agrees with this interpretation  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 17 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab and  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm fragment of yellow red  firm breast tissue with localizing wire in place  Inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 0cm firm  poorly circumscribed stellate lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  Representative portion frozen as frozen section  1  now A  The remainder submitted in B through H  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Jeffrey Field Bleakley  M D  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
