Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  10 AUG 94 at 16 20 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  60   POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  INVASIVE AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  40   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 0 8cm in greatest diameter and extends to the surgical resection margin  No vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD Signed On  15 AUG 94 at 16 24                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 AUG 94 at 15 11     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan yellow  rubbery piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a white rubbery well circumscribed moveable mass  measuring 0 9cm in greatest diameter  No frozen section done  Representative sections are submitted in A through J  The sections of the well circumscribed mass are in E and F  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST   SMALL  0 9CM  FREELY MOVABLE NODULE AT PERIPHERY SOFT IN CONSISTENCY  NO OTHER LESION  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
