ut surface  The specimen was entirely submitted as frozen sections  3 and 4  and is now resubmitted as cassette C and D  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 5cm breast with REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 6cm of attached axilla  The attached skin measures REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm areola and a REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm nipple  The skin is stained with blue ink  A stitch marks the highest lymph node in the axillary tissue  There is no nipple or skin retraction and the specimen is otherwise externally unremarkable  The deep margin of the specimen is inked in black and sectioned to reveal a focus of the tissue which is dyed blue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  A firm white yellow mass is identified towards the medial aspect of the specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  This mass extends to within 2 3cm of the deep  posterior  margin of the specimen  The breast parenchyma is otherwise composed of unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  The axillary tissue was extensively searched for lymph nodes and 17 were identified  The axillary lymph nodes range from REMOVED_DATE to 1 8cm in greatest diameter  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Cassette E  highest  most superior   lymph node in axillary region  Cassettes F O  axillary lymph nodes  Cassettes P R  representative sections of mass  Cassette S  mass in relation to closest margin   deep margin   Cassettes T V  representative sections of mass  Cassette W  representative section away from the tumor towards the medial aspect of the specimen  Cassette X  representative section of tissue away from the tumor  towards the lateral aspect of the specimen  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mastectomy margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x 7 1cm donut shaped portion of skin which is externally unremarkable  The specimen is un oriented