Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 58 CLINICAL DATA  56 year old female with left breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   ADENOCARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  INVASIVE GRADE III III  FOCALLY MUCIN SECRETORY  REMOVED_DATE CM IN MAXIMUM DIMENSION  NOTE  Several foci of tumor in lymphatic spaces are identified  Tumor is present in 1 of 6 lymph nodes  Representative sections from the margins are free of tumor  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  04 MAY 95 at 15 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 MAY 95 at 07 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm modified breast radical mastectomy specimen  which includes a REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm axillary tail  On the specimen there is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm skin ellipse with a 0 9cm in diameter nipple and a 2 5cm in diameter areolar complex  2 5cm from the superior skin margin  on the skin ellipse is a 0 6cm suture  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm  On cross section  there is an area of firm  white tissue that is directly underneath the skin suture previously noted  This area of white  firm tissue measures a 5 0cm in width and 5 0cm in superior inferior dimension  It comes to within 1 5cm of the closest deep margin  2 5cm from the closest inferior margin  and 5 0cm from the superior margin  In this area of white  firm tissue there are areas of focal hemorrhage  There is no biopsy cavity present  SECTION CODE  A  tumor with closest deep inked margin  B D  tumor with deep inked margin  E  most lateral extension of the tumor  F  area of white  fibrous bands  medial and discontinuous with the medial extent of the tumor  G  representative section from the biopsy site  H  representative section through the nipple with underlying breast  I  skin with suture and underlying breast  J L  additional dissected lymph nodes  M  representative section from the medial margin  N  representative section from the superior margin  O  representative section from the inferior margin  P  representative section from the lateral aspect of the skin ellipse  Resident  M  Priscilla Short  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  26 AUG 94 at 11 29 CLINICAL DATA  72 year old female with a history of right breast cancer with mastectomy   REMOVED_CASE_ID    she now has dimpling of the left nipple  Biopsy  left breast diagnosed intraductal carcinoma  REMOVED_CASE_ID  treated with radiation only                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY OF LARGE MASS  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  INVOLVING THE ENTIRE BIOPSY SPECIMEN INCLUDING THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 94 at 14 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of breast tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm ellipse of unremarkable overlying skin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 9cm in greatest diameter white tan  hard scirrhous nodule grossly involving the resection margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and kept frozen for Cox 5  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in cassettes A through D  with cassette A having the majority of the nodule  The skin is submitted in D  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   INFILTRATING MAMMARY CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  Carlos Fernandez del castillo  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
