Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 59 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer on needle biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR MARGIN  SEE NOTE   LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MULTIFOCAL  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  FOCALLY PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE POSTERIOR MARGIN  BREAST   FINAL SHAVED MARGINS    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  RESIDUAL INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  LYMPH NODE   LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL NODE    EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE FREE OF CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  ALL  10  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  BREAST   ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGINS    EXCISONAL BIOPSY  BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 18 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast infiltrated with blue dye and entirely inked black  The superior aspect is overinked yellow  the posterior is overinked blue  the specimen is serially section from lateral to medial to reveal a 1 2cm tan gray firm mass  0 3cm from the anterior margin  1 0cm from the posterior margin  Section code  A B  Mass relative to anterior margin C  Mass relative to posterior margin D  Additional section of mass with anterior and posterior margins E  Additional section of posterior margin F  Additional normal breast parenchyma  Received fresh and  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axilla sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm piece of adipose and lymphoid tissue  which is bisected and entirely submitted in Cassettes O and P  Also received fresh and  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of adipose tissue  from which multiple lymph nodes are identified  These range fro