ning of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast mass  is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  fibrofatty tissue fragment with two stitches  one short  superior  and one long  lateral   Inked and sectioned to reveal a hard  tan white mass centrally  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The mass is 0 6cm  from the nearest margin which is anterior  Radial margin laterally at the long stitch in A  Radial margin superiorly at the short stitch in B  The superior portion of the tissue fragment submitted lateral to medial in C E G J L N  and P  The inferior portion of the fragment submitted from lateral to medial in D F H I K M O  and Q  A representative fragment of tumor is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Hormone receptors taken  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  fragment is given for research  Labeled with patient s unit number  right axilla nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm fibroadipose tissue fragment containing multiple lymph nodes  pink tan  REMOVED_DATE to 1 8cm in diameter  Lymph nodes in R through W  Resident  William H  Yong  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION  COLLOID CARCINOMA  INKED MARGINS GROSSLY FREE OF TUMOR  O R  Resident  James Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOW