Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 19 02 CLINICAL DATA  Status post lumpectomy and radiation for breast carcinoma nine years ago  now with local recurrence and TRAM breast reconstruction                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  TWO FOCI  BIOPSY CAVITY   SEE NOTE  2  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  FIBROSIS  AND FAT NECROSIS  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  4  SKIN WITH SCAR  SKIN AND SOFT TISSUE  ABDOMEN   EXCISION  SKIN AND FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  NOTE  The resection margins are free of carcinoma  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 06 55                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left simple mastectomy  is a 450 gram mastectomy specimen  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm  An overlying skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm  and contains a 6 0cm linear incision in the upper outer quadrant  The nipple is slightly retracted and measures 0 8cm in greatest dimension  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm red fluid filled cyst  extending to within 0 3cm of the overlying skin incision and to within 0 4cm of the deep resection margin  The wall of the capsule is irregular and tan and measures 0 2cm in thickness  The surrounding tissue is firm and tan  The remainder of the parenchyma is yellow and grossly unremarkable  Section Code A   deep resection margin with biopsy cavity  representative sections B   biopsy cavity with superficial resection margin C H   biopsy cavity  representative radial sections I J   breast  representative sections K   skin with scar  representative sections L M   nipple  trisected  submitted in entirety Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  abdominal tissue  is  REMOVED_CASE_ID  grams of fibroadipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  Some of the fragments contain irregular skin ellipses  ranging in size from 10 x 3cm to 5 x 5cm  Sectioning reveals no gross lesions Section Code N  O    abdominal tissue   representative sections Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  G Gregory Gallico III  M D  PART A  LEFT SIMPLE MASECTOMY PART B  ABDOMINAL TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 10 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 3 OF 3  EXTENDING TO AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  WITH METASTASIS TO AN INTRA PARENCHYMAL LYMPH NODE  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  In situ carcinoma is not identified  Estrogen and progesterone receptor status will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm nodule of breast tissue with a well demarcated  irregular firm and gritty white to gray nodule  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm in size abutting an inked resection margin  A portion of the suspicious nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  submitted entirely in A through I  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST RIGHT EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 52 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  FORMING MANY NODULES THAT SPAN A REGION AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 17 OF 17 LYMPH NODES WITH EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 24                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a  REMOVED_CASE_ID  g  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm unoriented left mastectomy specimen  which includes a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm left axillary tail  and which is partially covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 11 7cm skin ellipse  The skin ellipse includes a 5 5cm in diameter areola with central nipple  and a recent 4 0cm in length  healing scar  running 8 5cm superolateral to the nipple  The remainder of the skin is diffusely tan white and otherwise unremarkable  The deep resection margin is a smooth plane  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a prior REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm biopsy site  characterized by sulfur yellow discoloration  located immediately subjacent to the epidermal incision  This biopsy cavity approaches to within 1 5cm of the superior margin  4 5cm of the deep inked margin  6 5cm of the inferior margin  and is distant from both the lateral and medial margins  The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of mature  lobular  yellow  adipose tissue with thick  intercollating  fibrous bands  The axillary tail is explored for lymph nodes  Several lymph nodes are identified  Section Code  A  biopsy cavity with scar and superior margin  B  deep inked margin overlying biopsy site  C D  remainder of biopsy site  E G  fibrotic areas near biopsy site  H I  fibrosis at deep inked margin inferior to biopsy site  J  fibrosis at inferior margin  K  nipple  L O  low nodes  P Q  middle nodes  R  high nodes  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
