Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 03 CLINICAL DATA  Right modified radical mastectomy for stage III ductal carcinoma  Biopsy was positive for estrogen and progesterone receptors  Patient given preoperative chemotherapy  cytoxan  methotrexate  and 5 FU                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA OF BREAST  95    AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    WITH FOCAL COMEDO FEATURES  EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION  INTRAMAMMARY AND INTRADERMALLY  20 OF 23 LYMPH NODES ARE POSITIVE FOR CARCINOMA   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Areas of tumor are poorly differentiated  Two nodules of metastatic tumor in the axillary fat have no lymphoid architecture and are in addition to the nodes above  Several small veins surrounding some of the lymph nodes also contain intraluminal carcinoma cells  There are several small foci of malignant cells identified at the inked deep resection margin  No pagetoid cells are found in the epidermis on H and E and on PAS stain  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 29                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 10 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen  measuring 15 x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm with an attached axillary tail measuring 10 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  There is an overlying ellipse of skin  measuring 16 x 7 cm with a linear depression of skin at the lateral superior areolar margin    scar   Located 5cm from the medial tip of the skin ellipse and 2cm from the superior aspect of the skin ellipse is a 3 0cm areola with a 0 8cm nipple  Underlying the linear depression at the margin of the areola is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fibrous area  Just deep to this fibrous area is a cream colored  hard mass  2 5cm from the deep resection margin   The mass measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  A second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm firm  white yellow mass is apparent in the superomedial deep aspect of the specimen  1 0cm from the proximal deep resection margin   There is a 9 x 9 x 5cm round  fibrous area present beneath the center of the skin ellipse  admixed with fat  SECTION CODE  A G  multiple rubbery to firm  white tan nodules  0 2 to 2 5cm    H K  representative sections of mass underlying fibrous scar  L N  representative sections of mass from the superomedial aspect of the breast  deep   O  grossly normal breast tissue  P  rubbery mass  beneath center of the ellipse   Q  nipple  R  biopsy scar  S X  Resident  Karen C  Deering  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  David L Gibbs  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
