esent fibrotic or fibrocystic non tumorous tissue  The lesion has a firm pink white cut surface with a central punctate region of hemorrhage suggestive of prior biopsy site  The lesion extends to 1 0cm from the medial margin  1 2cm from the lateral margin  2 1cm from the superior margin  0 8cm from the anterior margin  and grossly extends to both the posterior and inferior margins  The remaining tissue is composed of grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma  The specimen is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin  bisected  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lesion to closest superior margin  green    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lesion to closest anterior margin  blue    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest posterior and inferior margins  grossly positive  black   yellow    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional grossly positive posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lesion closest to medial margin  medial margin 1 0cm away    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lesion closest to lateral margin  lateral margin 1 2cm away    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Grossly unremarkable parenchyma  Received fresh and labeled  right breast superior final margin   are unoriented soft tissue fragments aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh and labeled  right breast final inferior margin   are multiple unoriented soft tissue fragments aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh and labeled  right breast final medial margin   are multiple unoriented soft tissue fragments aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  in container labeled  right breast  final inferior margin   requisition designated  right breast final lateral margin   are multiple unoriented soft tissue fragments aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   SENTINEL NODE  HOT   BLUE    REMOVED_CASE_ID    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2    2A   BLUE NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 30   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 27 14PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erbB 2 Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows    Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells    Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells    Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 02   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 44 13PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnose