ors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a 14 x 16 x 7 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an 11 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  and a 15 x 7 0cm skin ellipse with a nipple in the center  A firm mass is palpable directly below the nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 7 x 6 x 6cm relatively well circumscribed tan to yellow nodular mass with focal cystic and soft regions  the largest cyst is 3cm in diameter and contains bloody fluid  The nodular mass grossly abuts against the posterior and inferior resection margin  Four representative sections of the mass are submitted in cassettes A through D  the closest margin  deep  is submitted in A  A representative section of a tan white  fibrous area that extends from the tumor to the inferior resection margin is submitted in cassette E  Similar fibrous tissue on the posterior deep resection margin is submitted in cassette F  which also contains another section of the fibrous tissue  Dissection of the axillary tail yielded multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from 0 3cm to 2 0cm  submitted in cassettes G through L  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Armaghan A Mostafavi  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
