REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm defect  which is inked yellow   The anterior margin of the specimen is inked blue and the posterior margin is  inked black  Sectioning reveals an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 9 4cm irregular tan  multinodular and firm mass that almost entirely replaces the breast parenchyma    ulcerates through the skin at multiple foci  Further sectioning reveals  focal hemorrhage   necrosis    the mass abuts the anterior and posterior  margins  The mass comes to 0 1cm of the medial  0 3cm of the lateral  0 7cm  of the superior    1 0cm of the inferior skin margins  The remainder of the  specimen consists of minimal yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The axillary tail  is palpated and sectioned to reveal multiple candidate lymph nodes ranging from  0 2 to 4 5cm in greatest dimension  Several appear grossly positive and the  largest candidate is multinodular and is consistent with several matted lymph  nodes  Gross photographs are taken   representative sections are submitted as  follows      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to include skin ulceration    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to include superior skin margin   anterior margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to include inferior skin margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative medial skin margin  radial    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative lateral skin margin  radial    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to include posterior margin  defect in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative mass to include nodular skin in cassettes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional mass to include possible lymph node    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Candidate lymph nodes    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Six intact lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two intact lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two intact lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Grossly positive node  representative   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Candidate node  representative   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lymph node  bisected  