egion of the invasive carcinoma  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2 and 3  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to  0 1cm from all the margins  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested  although there may be insufficient invasive tumor remaining for analysis  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm oriented breast tissue with two needle localization wires in place  a short stitch designating  superior   and long stitch designating  lateral   The long axis is anterior to posterior  and the specimen is inked as follows  Superior   blue  inferior   black  medial   green  lateral   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a 0 6cm gritty area  as well as hemorrhagic fibroadipose breast tissue  The gritty area is 0 2cm from the closest superior margin  0 4cm from the closest medial margin  0 7cm from the nearest inferior margin  and 1 2cm from the nearest lateral margin  It is 0 5cm from the anterior surface and 1 5cm from the posterior surface  The specimen is submitted entirely from anterior to posterior in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the gritty area in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  No invasive tumor cells are seen on the tissue sections stained for hormone receptors and HER 2  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the t