Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 35 CLINICAL DATA  34 year old woman with prior left breast cancer and known metastatic disease  Now with a right breast mass and supicious FNA                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASS    INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  FORMING MANY NODULES AS LARGE AS REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION THROUGHOUT SPECIMEN  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN IN SEVERAL FOCI  SEE NOTE  BREAST  RIGHT   7 O CLOCK    INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor appears similar to the cancer resected from the patient s left breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 48                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   7 O CLOCK    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 53     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR C ERB  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PROTEIN AS REPORTED BY IMPATH BREAST  RIGHT   Five percent  5   of the tumor cells stain for c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   favorable   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast tissue  Inked as follows  lateral  long stitch  black  superior  short  green  inferior yellow  anterior red  posterior blue  and medial black  The specimen is sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal multiple hard  white tan  well circumscribed nodules abutting the red inked margin  Frozen section of one of the nodules is FX 1 and saved frozen to Cox 5  An additional piece of tissue is saved  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted in cassettes A through E  Lateral margin is in cassette A  Medial margin in cassette E  Labeled  right breast 7 o clock  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of breast tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm yellow tan well circumscribed mass  entirely submitted in cassette F and G  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                       