Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  MS 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   CASE  MS 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient  MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE  Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1  Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D   Resident  Michiya Nishino  M D   Frozen Section Pathologist  Judith A Ferry  M D   Frozen Section Resident  Jessica Wang  M D   Signed Out by  John H Eichhorn  M D              Addended Report                Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results  Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH   Results  CLINICAL DATA   Right poorly differentiated  invasive ductal carcinoma  ER PR Her 2 negative   Status post neoadjuvant chemotherapy       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   RESIDUAL INVASIVE MAMMARY CARCINOMA  WITH NEOADJUVANT TREATMENT EFFECT     NOTE  The residual cancer is mostly present in a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm mass   gross measurement  that is composed of a central partly organized hematoma  surrounded by a dense shell of sclerotic  edematous  partly necrotic  and  slightly chronically inflamed tissue with dystrophic calcification  The  residual tumor cells are few in number and are scattered in this peripheral  shell of tissue  as isolated single and compact clusters of large epithelioid  cells with bizarre nuclear characteristics  with some mitotic activity   Abutting the mass is a hyalinized fibroepithelial lesion with dystrophic  calcification and also regions of residual carcinoma cells  both invasive and  in situ   probably representing a fibroadenoma partially involved by tumor   The neoplastic cells appears to be grade 2 to 3  but the evaluation of grade  and overall tumor size is hampered by the prior administration of chemotherapy   The tumor cells are within 0 1cm of the posterior margin  Parenchyma away  from the mass appears atrophic  This case also was reviewed at an MGH breast  pathology division conference on REMOVED_DATE     The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone  receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ  hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  will be  reported in an addendum     BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR FLAP   EXCISION   UNREMARKABLE FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY     LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   EXCISION   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWO OF TWO NODES  0 2   SEE NOTE   THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED     NOTE  To evaluate for metastatic carcinoma  immunohistochemical stains for  cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin were examined on levels  from each of three blocks  The findings support the above diagnosis     GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received are 3 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN     Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  right axillary sentinel  node   are 2 lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm   respectively  The smaller lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1   now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The larger lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1A  now  as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining fibroadipose tissue is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 8 2cm  mastectomy  specimen with a suture designating the 12 o clock position  A REMOVED_DATE x 10 5cm   ellipse of skin overlies a round  fluctuant mass in the upper outer quadrant   externally measuring 10cm in greatest dimension and spanning from the 7  o clock to 11 o clock position  and extending from the lateral aspect of the  areolus to 11 5cm from the nipple  A 0 4cm  well healed scar overl